task_spec.prompt:
The Rust library in src/lib.rs has word_count and capitalize_words as free functions. Refactor by extracting two traits:

pub trait TextAnalyzer {
    fn word_count(&self) -> usize;
}

pub trait TextFormatter {
    fn capitalize(&self) -> String;
}

Implement both traits for str:
  impl TextAnalyzer for str { fn word_count(&self) -> usize { word_count(self) } }
  impl TextFormatter for str { fn capitalize(&self) -> String { capitalize_words(self) } }

Keep the free functions (word_count, capitalize_words) unchanged.

Write a generic function:
  pub fn describe<T: TextAnalyzer + TextFormatter>(text: &T) -> String
  Returns a String of the form "{N} words: {capitalized}" where N = text.word_count() and capitalized = text.capitalize().

Write 4 tests:
  test_trait_word_count — "hello world".word_count() == 2
  test_trait_capitalize — "hello world".capitalize() == "Hello World"
  test_describe — describe("hello world") == "2 words: Hello World"
  test_describe_empty — describe("") == "0 words: "

All 3 original tests must still pass. cargo test must pass all 7 tests. cargo build must succeed.
